.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt LIBCAPBUNDLE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libcapbundle
.Nd parse and validate capability bundles
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libcapbundle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libcapbundle.h
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_open "const char *path" "struct capbundle **bp" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft void
.Fn capbundle_close "struct capbundle *b"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_verify "const struct capbundle *b" "char *errbuf" "size_t errlen"
.Ft int
.Fn capbundle_scan_dir "const char *path" "capbundle_scan_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
parses the two-level capability bundle format used by
.Xr switchboard 8 .
A bundle has one
.Pa Bundle.ucl
and an exact inventory of
.Pa Units/name.unit/Unit.ucl
process manifests and
.Pa Units/name.unit/bin/name
executables.
Identity, publisher metadata, and version ordering are bundle
fields; the program, user, activation, restart policy, resource limits, and
umask are unit fields.
.Pp
Parsing is literal and closed.
Unknown or duplicate keys, includes, macros, variables, implicit arrays,
invalid names, and entries beyond fixed limits are rejected.
Activation is explicit under
.Va activation.boot ,
.Va activation.ipc ,
.Va activation.timer
.Pq an object with a monotonic Va interval in seconds ,
.Va activation.schedule
.Pq a calendar cron string or named alias, optionally with Va persistent ,
.Va activation.path
.Pq an object with an absolute Va path watched for change events ,
.Va activation.queue_directory ,
.Va activation.on_mount ,
and
.Va activation.socket .
A monotonic
.Va timer
and a wall-clock
.Va schedule
are mutually exclusive.
.Pp
.Fn capbundle_verify
checks the exact tree shape, executable type and mode, activation triggers,
name uniqueness, and resource limits.
.Sh ACCESSORS
The public header exposes immutable accessors for bundle identity, display
version, sequence, author, publisher, path, unit count, unit labels,
activation, IPC names, timer interval, activation path, arguments,
environment, and conversion to
.Vt struct svc_manifest .
Returned strings remain owned by the bundle.
.Pp
IPC anointments are exposed per unit:
.Fn capbundle_svc_nrequires "s" "provides_idx"
and
.Fn capbundle_svc_requires "s" "provides_idx" "j"
walk the anointment names a connecting program must hold to resolve the
unit's
.Fa provides_idx Ns th
IPC name (zero names means the endpoint is open);
.Fn capbundle_svc_nanointments "s"
and
.Fn capbundle_svc_anointment "s" "i"
walk the names the unit itself declares it holds; and
.Fn capbundle_svc_provides_index "s" "name"
returns the index of the IPC name
.Fa name
or \-1 when the unit does not publish it.
Both lists are validated at parse time: reverse-domain names, unique, at most
.Dv CAPBUNDLE_MAX_REQUIRES
per endpoint and
.Dv CAPBUNDLE_MAX_ANOINTMENTS
per unit, and never the wildcard
.Dq * .
.Pp
The principal policy is exposed through
.Fn capbundle_principal_resolve ,
which fills a
.Vt struct capbundle_principal_grant
with the anointments a login session holds, the names it may elevate to, and
whether it carries admin rights, per
.Pa /Capabilities/Config/principal-policy.ucl ;
.Fn capbundle_principal_holds
and
.Fn capbundle_principal_may_elevate
query a grant.
An absent or malformed policy applies the historical root-or-wheel rule and
sets
.Fa from_default_rule .
.Sh TRUST
.Nm
rejects symlinks and special objects but does not establish ownership policy.
.Xr switchboard 8
requires registry trees to be root-owned and not group/world writable.
.Xr switchboardctl 8
normalizes and atomically publishes staged installations.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt int
return zero on success and -1 on failure.
When supplied, the error buffer receives an administrative diagnostic.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr switchboard 5 ,
.Xr switchboard 8 ,
.Xr switchboardctl 8
